// The trailer, v6 (#1178): Tools/trailer-cut.py Tools/trailer/trailer.json
// The owner's verdict on v5 (2026-11-20): the trailer looks good; the music swells in at the start; no skip hint in the first shot;
// and, most of all, the gun MOVES wherever the game is played - round the island (turn=) and in and out (walk=) - since that is why
// the game is 3D: it fires from different positions, in the last shot too, and may fire while moving.
// A HUD clip is never filmed with the benchmark's gun (its lens circles the gun): the shots it found are replayed by "hands" with the
// game's own camera. A shot found from a gun a script moves needs the same moves in the replay: a turn held as long, from rest, ends
// on the same bearing whenever it starts. Camera paths count from a clip's window start, a quarter second before its "in".
